        "ja": "カジッチュ",
        "ko": "과사삭벌레",
        "ja-Hrkt": "カジッチュ",
        "zh-Hans": "啃果虫",
        "zh-Hant": "啃果蟲"
      },
      "description": {
        "fun": "A tiny dragon that lives its whole life inside an apple, which is its home, its food and its disguise from hungry bird Pokémon. It's the lightest and shortest Dragon-type of all. In Galar, giving someone an Applin is a romantic gesture, and the flavour of its apple decides what it becomes: tart, sweet or syrupy.",
        "guide": "A tiny Grass and Dragon-type Pokémon that burrows into an apple at birth and uses it as home, food and disguise. Applin evolves into Flapple, Appletun or Dipplin depending on the apple it is given.",
        "tagline": "A pocket-sized dragon hiding inside an apple",
        "sources": [
          {
            "title": "Bulbapedia: Applin (Pokémon)",
            "url": "https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Applin_(Pok%C3%A9mon)"
          }
        ]
      },
      "branches": {
        "text": "The apple decides. A Tart Apple makes the flying, acid-spitting Flapple; a Sweet Apple makes the pie-backed Appletun; and the Syrupy Apple, grown only in Kitakami and added in The Teal Mask, makes Dipplin, which can go on to become Hydrapple.",
        "sources": [
          {
            "title": "Bulbapedia: Applin (Pokémon)",
            "url": "https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Applin_(Pok%C3%A9mon)"
          },
          {
            "title": "Bulbapedia: Dipplin (Pokémon)",
            "url": "https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Dipplin_(Pok%C3%A9mon)"
          }
        ]
      },
