        "ko": "과미드라",
        "ja-Hrkt": "カミツオロチ",
        "zh-Hans": "蜜集大蛇",
        "zh-Hant": "蜜集大蛇"
      },
      "description": {
        "fun": "Seven 'syrpents' living in an apple made of syrup, led by the one in the middle. They're fickle and rarely agree, but on the rare occasion their moods line up, Hydrapple unleashes its true power. Its design draws on many-headed dragons like the Hydra and Japan's Yamata no Orochi, and it's the only member of its family to reach a third stage.",
        "guide": "The evolution of Dipplin, introduced in The Indigo Disk. Hydrapple is made of seven serpent-like creatures inside a syrup apple, commanded by the central one, and is inspired by many-headed dragons such as the Hydra.",
        "tagline": "Seven moody serpents in one syrup apple",
        "sources": [
          {
            "title": "Bulbapedia: Hydrapple (Pokémon)",
            "url": "https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Hydrapple_(Pok%C3%A9mon)"
          }
        ]
      },
